  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington is underperforming against calendar-adjusted expectations, while Hicksville is tracking worse operationally. Glen Cove is running strong but has a scheduling crisis that needs immediate attention.\n\nPort Washington revenue is down 27% month-to-date, but the calendar adjustment tells the real story: you're only 5% below expectation through November 3rd. The miss is real but modest. What concerns me more is capacity: you're running 4.0 groomer-days per day this month versus 5.3 last October, and yesterday's 5 groomers produced $474 per head against a trailing-30-day baseline of $489. The team isn't the problem\u2014scheduling is. You're also seeing early warning signs in visit cadence: add-on attachment dropped from 54% to 50% and retail comps were flat week-over-week. Both are operational signals worth monitoring.\n\nHicksville is your real problem. DOW-adjusted, you're actually running 40% *ahead* of expectation through the 3rd\u2014calendar is helping, not hurting. But the operational picture is dire. Groomer-days are down 46% month-over-month (2.0 vs 3.7 per day), productivity per groomer is down 21% ($357 vs $452), and retail cratered 58% yesterday. Zero bather hours scheduled all month signals either a staffing gap or a scheduling miss. Appointments are down 49% YTD versus prior month's period. This is a capacity and cross-selling collapse, not demand.\n\nGlen Cove is your bright spot\u2014up 87% versus DOW-adjusted expectation\u2014but you have *zero* groomers scheduled for today and tomorrow and *zero* groomer-days booked for the next 7 days. This is a scheduling error, not success. Fix it immediately or you'll squander momentum.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Port Washington has 7 groomers and 15.0 bather-hours scheduled today and tomorrow; Hicksville has 4\u20135 groomers and zero bathers; Glen Cove is dark for the next 7 days (0 groomer-days) and must be rescheduled; across both main locations, 36 groomer-days are scheduled for the next 7 days, down sharply from prior month's run-rate.**"
